AB  - Supply chain problems are becoming multifaceted in the present dynamic and competitive market landscape. Hence, it is necessary to streamline the operations and make them agile, flexible, and highly responsive. Thus, machine learning in supply chain activities has emerged exponentially during the last decade and has positively impacted organizational performance. In the scholarly literature, machine learning is reported as a game-changer and facilitates effective decision-making, cost minimization, and enhanced overall performance. Despite the available literature, research works on machine learning applications and their implementation in core supply chain functions, including stakeholders’ collaboration, inventory management, and demand forecasting, are limited. Therefore, an inclusive literature review is required to acknowledge and analyze the importance of using machine learning in supply chain activities. To achieve this, we searched the Scopus database for papers related to the use of machine learning on supply chain performance. After a careful examination and thorough study, 53 papers were selected. Moreover, the presented research applied the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses framework and a comprehensive literature review. In descriptive analysis, the research articles were analyzed according to the publication years, publication journals, countries focused on, industries focused on, citations of articles, and focused areas in supply chain management. Moreover, a Bibliometric analysis was conducted, which shows a strong inclination of industry professionals and practitioners toward adopting machine learning in supply chain activities. Network analysis further identified five themes, i.e., supply chain risk management, supply chain inventory management, supply chain demand forecasting, supply chain supplier selection, and supply chain collaboration. Furthermore, several actionable future research directions have been proposed for future studies to improve supply chain management sustainability.
